1. _Proof / _Thm / _ATP wrappers (~lines 1297-1895)
   Nearly every core lemma has 1-3 trivial copies with a _Proof, _Thm, or _ATP
   suffix whose body is just `exact?`, `convert ... using 1`, or a direct call
   to the original. ~40 such wrappers exist, e.g.:
     ReachableCount_Zero / ReachableCount_Zero_Proof / ReachableCount_Zero_Thm / ReachableCount_Zero_Proof_2
     FiniteBoundedTape / FiniteBoundedTape_Proof
     step_eq_NextConfig / step_eq_NextConfig_Proof / step_eq_NextConfig_ATP
     FiniteEdges / FiniteEdges_Proof / FiniteEdges_ATP
     ImmermanWitness_Correct / ImmermanWitness_Correct_Proof / ImmermanWitness_Theorem / ImmermanWitness_Theorem_ATP
     NSPACE_Closed_Under_Complement_Conditional / _Proof / _Proof_2 / _Proof_3 / _Thm
   ACTION: Delete all _Proof/_Thm/_ATP duplicates; update any call sites to
   use the original lemma directly.

2. DualMachine variants (lines 2067-2141)
   DualMachine, DualMachine_v3, DualMachine_v4 define nearly the same machine
   with minor state-type differences (Option vs Sum). Only DualMachine_v4 style
   (Sum) is arguably needed, since NormalizedTM_v2 supersedes them all.
   ACTION: Keep only the one actually used (none are referenced later); delete
   the rest.

3. NormalizedTM / NormalizedTM_v2 (lines 2207-2260)
   NormalizedTM and NormalizedTM_v2 are character-for-character identical.
   ACTION: Delete NormalizedTM; rename NormalizedTM_v2 to NormalizedTM.

4. AcceptsCoN_imp_NormalizedTM_v2_AcceptsCoN x3 (lines 2441-2537)
   Three versions: the original, _v2 (body is `exact?`), and _v3 (calls _v2).
   ACTION: Keep one; delete the other two.

5. Repeated Nat.log2 helper lemmas (lines 1207-1259, 1397-1412)
   Nat.log2_mul_le / Nat.log2_mul_le_Proof
   Nat.log2_pow_le / Nat.log2_pow_le_Proof
   Nat.log2_mul3_le / Nat.log2_mul3_le_Proof
   ACTION: Delete the _Proof copies.

6. Exists_Minimal_Chain / ListChain_imp_NodupListChain duplication (lines 931-960, 1577-1635)
   Both the original and _Proof versions contain the same Nat.find-based proof
   inlined. Factor the Nat.find argument into a small helper or keep only one copy.

7. Harmonic generalize_proofs tactic (lines 1-227)
   ~225 lines of boilerplate for a custom tactic. If Mathlib's built-in
   generalize_proofs suffices, this can be removed entirely.
